WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.833 --> 00:00:07.963
Hi, I'm Melissa Villaseñor,
and I do voice impressions.

00:00:08.004 --> 00:00:09.714
For example,

00:00:09.756 --> 00:00:12.884
this is Kristen Wiig
about to go skydiving.

00:00:14.844 --> 00:00:16.888
“I changed my mind.

00:00:17.847 --> 00:00:20.850
I'm, I'm scared, I'm scared
I'll get stuck on a cloud,

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.103
and then I’ll have to 
become an angel.”

00:00:23.103 --> 00:00:25.897
(Laughter and applause)

00:00:25.897 --> 00:00:27.065
Thanks.

00:00:27.816 --> 00:00:29.651
This is Sandra Bullock

00:00:29.651 --> 00:00:32.195
if she were to knock over
a bunch of dominoes.

00:00:32.237 --> 00:00:34.197
Just pretend they're here in the room.

00:00:34.656 --> 00:00:36.783
“No, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no.”

00:00:36.783 --> 00:00:37.951
That's it.

00:00:37.993 --> 00:00:38.994
(Laughter)

00:00:38.994 --> 00:00:40.745
She always does that in movies.

00:00:40.787 --> 00:00:42.330
And this is Lady Gaga

00:00:42.372 --> 00:00:45.333
if she gave birth to a baby
in "A Star is Born."

00:00:46.376 --> 00:00:53.008
(Vocalizing)

00:00:58.597 --> 00:01:00.307
(Vocalizing baby crying)

00:01:00.307 --> 00:01:02.976
(Applause and laughter)

00:01:03.018 --> 00:01:04.894
Miss Gaga, a star is born.

00:01:04.936 --> 00:01:07.230
(Laughter)

00:01:07.272 --> 00:01:10.942
And this is Melissa Villaseñor
giving a TED Talk.

00:01:10.942 --> 00:01:14.070
Hi, I'm Melissa Villaseñor
and I do voice impressions.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.488
(Laughter)

00:01:15.488 --> 00:01:16.948
A little bit about me.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.326
Born and raised
in Los Angeles, California,

00:01:19.326 --> 00:01:21.536
to a Mexican-American family.

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:25.081
Middle child, OK, I was very shy.

00:01:25.081 --> 00:01:27.459
I didn't do the best in school,

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.587
but I was very observant,
maybe a little creepy.

00:01:30.629 --> 00:01:34.132
And I realized I had this superpower
of doing voice impressions

00:01:34.174 --> 00:01:35.925
when I was 12 years old.

00:01:35.925 --> 00:01:39.179
And it all began with the pop
singers at that time, OK.

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:40.388
Britney Spears:

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:44.017
“All you people look at me
like I’m a little girl.”

00:01:44.851 --> 00:01:46.853
I know, spooky.

00:01:46.853 --> 00:01:49.314
(Laughter)

00:01:49.356 --> 00:01:50.523
And hot.

00:01:50.565 --> 00:01:52.275
I should do that all the time, huh?

00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:53.985
(Laughter)

00:01:54.361 --> 00:01:57.155
I sang a lot of Shakira back then, just,

00:01:57.197 --> 00:02:00.533
“There’s a she wolf in the closet.”

00:02:00.533 --> 00:02:04.704
And I was kind of wolf-like singing at 13,
you know, hairy, puberty days.

00:02:04.746 --> 00:02:06.665
(Laughter)

00:02:06.706 --> 00:02:09.125
I looked up to Gwen Stefani
in high school.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:13.088
I loved Gwen Stefani from No Doubt,
and I wanted to look like her.

00:02:13.088 --> 00:02:15.590
So I shaved my eyebrows
real thin to copy her,

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:18.593
like in the "Return of Saturn"
days, that Gwen.

00:02:18.635 --> 00:02:21.137
And I thought, "Oh, my friends
at school must think

00:02:21.179 --> 00:02:23.098
I look just like Gwen Stefani."

00:02:23.098 --> 00:02:25.392
I probably looked more like It, the clown.

00:02:25.433 --> 00:02:27.352
It was spooky, thin, just,

00:02:27.352 --> 00:02:30.814
“I kinda always knew
I’d end up looking like It.”

00:02:30.814 --> 00:02:33.525
(Laughter)

00:02:33.525 --> 00:02:36.945
I loved making my friends laugh
at school with my voices.

00:02:37.278 --> 00:02:39.280
And I suddenly wasn't so shy anymore.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.157
I felt like, oh, this is why I'm here.

00:02:41.157 --> 00:02:44.244
This is my purpose,
to bring joy and laughs.

00:02:44.285 --> 00:02:47.789
And I suddenly got obsessed
with Saturday Night Live at 15 years old.

00:02:47.831 --> 00:02:49.874
And I was so determined, I was like,

00:02:49.874 --> 00:02:51.334
I'm going to become a comedian

00:02:51.376 --> 00:02:54.003
and I'm going to get on the cast
of Saturday Night Live.

00:02:54.003 --> 00:02:56.506
So right after high school, I graduate,

00:02:56.548 --> 00:03:00.051
I go straight to signing up
for open mic shows in Hollywood.

00:03:00.051 --> 00:03:03.471
My parents went straight
to worrying for their daughter.

00:03:03.471 --> 00:03:04.764
(Laughter)

00:03:04.806 --> 00:03:06.766
Now I went to junior college for them.

00:03:06.808 --> 00:03:09.894
You know, I went for, like,
a quarter or a semester.

00:03:09.894 --> 00:03:12.397
I don't know, I wasn't there
long enough to find out.

00:03:12.439 --> 00:03:13.982
(Laughter)

00:03:14.023 --> 00:03:17.694
But thankfully I got amazing opportunities
pretty early on in my career

00:03:17.694 --> 00:03:21.656
because I think it was rare to see
a female voice impressionist

00:03:21.656 --> 00:03:22.824
at comedy clubs.

00:03:22.824 --> 00:03:24.200
And a cute one.

00:03:24.284 --> 00:03:25.910
(Laughs)

00:03:27.954 --> 00:03:31.124
(Laughter)

00:03:31.124 --> 00:03:33.877
But I got the opportunity
to be on “America’s Got Talent”

00:03:33.877 --> 00:03:35.962
season six in 2011.

00:03:36.004 --> 00:03:39.215
I'm not going to lie,
I killed it, OK, 90 seconds.

00:03:39.591 --> 00:03:41.384
I did a bunch of impressions, just,

00:03:41.384 --> 00:03:42.844
Barbara Walters.

00:03:42.886 --> 00:03:46.806
I did a Natalie Portman
from the "Black Swan."

00:03:47.515 --> 00:03:50.727
I did a Sarah Silverman.

00:03:51.728 --> 00:03:53.271
Wanda Sykes.

00:03:54.147 --> 00:03:55.899
I did Miley Cyrus.

00:03:55.899 --> 00:03:59.903
And Christina Aguilera, oh, oh.

00:03:59.944 --> 00:04:01.863
(Laughter)

00:04:01.863 --> 00:04:03.823
From that exposure, being on that show,

00:04:03.823 --> 00:04:05.950
I was able to quit my part-time job

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.703
and become a headlining comedian
around the country

00:04:08.703 --> 00:04:10.246
for clubs and colleges.

00:04:10.288 --> 00:04:13.333
Now, that's amazing if you've been
doing stand up for a while,

00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:17.253
but I only had ten minutes
and suddenly I had to do an hour

00:04:17.295 --> 00:04:18.463
at comedy club.

00:04:18.505 --> 00:04:19.756
So I bombed a lot.

00:04:19.798 --> 00:04:22.717
I cried in a lot of hotels
around the country.

00:04:24.385 --> 00:04:26.513
But I noticed something
as I was on the road,

00:04:26.554 --> 00:04:28.097
working on jokes and performing,

00:04:28.097 --> 00:04:31.810
I noticed that everyone was laughing
at all the impression bits.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:35.772
But every time I tried to talk
about myself and my life, my family,

00:04:35.772 --> 00:04:38.316
it didn't get laughs
and it was starting to bug me.

00:04:38.316 --> 00:04:40.985
People will come up to me
after shows and they would go,

00:04:40.985 --> 00:04:43.238
"Oh, I love your Owen Wilson impression.

00:04:43.279 --> 00:04:45.114
He's so funny."

00:04:45.573 --> 00:04:47.116
And I'd say, "Thanks,"

00:04:47.158 --> 00:04:49.369
but inside I'd be like,

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.622
"Wait, do they only like me
for my Owen Wilson impression, wow?

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:56.084
That really bums me out, man."

00:04:56.125 --> 00:04:58.753
(Laughter)

00:04:58.753 --> 00:05:00.880
So at that point I became
determined again.

00:05:00.922 --> 00:05:03.174
I was like, no, I'm going
to write about myself.

00:05:03.174 --> 00:05:06.803
I want to find my own voice
among the voices that I do

00:05:06.845 --> 00:05:09.097
because I think it's important
and it's special,

00:05:09.138 --> 00:05:11.349
and I think it's the best
feeling to connect

00:05:11.349 --> 00:05:13.601
as your true self with other people.

00:05:15.228 --> 00:05:16.354
(Laughs)

00:05:16.354 --> 00:05:17.438
(Applause)

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:20.358
And, you know, thankfully,
I did find a voice.

00:05:20.358 --> 00:05:23.152
Yeah, a funny-sounding one, 
but a voice.

00:05:23.486 --> 00:05:25.405
And I like making fun of things in life.

00:05:25.446 --> 00:05:27.907
It just makes life
a little easier to handle.

00:05:27.949 --> 00:05:30.243
I like making fun of my energy.

00:05:30.285 --> 00:05:32.036
It's not sexy.

00:05:32.078 --> 00:05:33.204
You feel it.

00:05:33.246 --> 00:05:34.622
(Laughter)

00:05:34.664 --> 00:05:37.876
My energy is a lot like a proud dad's.

00:05:37.917 --> 00:05:40.211
(Laughter)

00:05:40.253 --> 00:05:42.255
No wonder relationships don't work out.

00:05:42.255 --> 00:05:43.923
Because every time I go on a date,

00:05:43.923 --> 00:05:45.800
I check out the dude, first thing I go,

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.260
"Man, look at you."

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.261
(Laughter)

00:05:48.303 --> 00:05:50.346
"Ah, you look good.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:51.848
Is that a new jacket?

00:05:51.848 --> 00:05:53.474
You look really sharp, my boy."

00:05:53.516 --> 00:05:55.268
(Laughter)

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.477
"Here's 20 bucks.

00:05:56.477 --> 00:05:57.979
Don't tell your mom, go ahead."

00:05:58.021 --> 00:05:59.147
(Laughter)

00:05:59.981 --> 00:06:02.525
I like talking about how
I'm Mexican, you know?

00:06:02.859 --> 00:06:05.403
And I don't look it,
a lot of people don't believe me.

00:06:05.445 --> 00:06:06.946
All my life, people would say,

00:06:06.988 --> 00:06:09.324
"Oh, you're Mexican?
You don't look Mexican."

00:06:09.365 --> 00:06:11.242
And I get so apologetic, I'm like,

00:06:11.284 --> 00:06:14.329
"Oh, I'm so sorry, I forgot my sombrero.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.705
Oh, man.

00:06:15.747 --> 00:06:18.333
Did I not roll my Rs enough? Sorry."

00:06:18.374 --> 00:06:20.084
And I just have to salsa away.

00:06:20.126 --> 00:06:21.920
(Laughter)

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.963
I know, exterior, you wouldn't believe it,

00:06:24.005 --> 00:06:26.507
but just know that inside ...

00:06:26.549 --> 00:06:28.259
A lot of piñatas in here.

00:06:28.301 --> 00:06:29.427
(Laughter)

00:06:29.469 --> 00:06:30.887
I bleed Tapatío.

00:06:30.929 --> 00:06:32.055
(Laughter)

00:06:33.431 --> 00:06:35.683
You know, I don't speak Spanish.

00:06:35.725 --> 00:06:37.352
I was a lazy kid,

00:06:37.352 --> 00:06:39.562
second generation Mexican,
I didn't work on it.

00:06:39.604 --> 00:06:41.564
I know, shame on me.

00:06:41.606 --> 00:06:43.858
Or as you would say in Spanish ...

00:06:44.233 --> 00:06:45.401
I don't know.

00:06:45.443 --> 00:06:48.363
(Laughter)

00:06:49.447 --> 00:06:51.407
I have been working on my Spanish though,

00:06:51.449 --> 00:06:54.744
because there's a lot of relatives of mine
that only speak in Spanish.

00:06:54.744 --> 00:06:58.247
And I think back when I would hang out
with my great grandma, my abuelita,

00:06:58.289 --> 00:07:01.542
you know, I would just nod
and smile and wave at her.

00:07:01.584 --> 00:07:02.752
How rude.

00:07:02.752 --> 00:07:05.964
But she didn't mind, she would just stare
at me lovingly, you know.

00:07:07.298 --> 00:07:09.801
I'd be like, "Hey, abuelita, how are you?"

00:07:10.551 --> 00:07:11.678
“Ay.”

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:18.726
(Speaking in Spanish)

00:07:19.852 --> 00:07:21.980
Thanks, you’re bonita, too.

00:07:22.021 --> 00:07:23.147
(Laughter)

00:07:23.189 --> 00:07:24.315
"Ay."

00:07:25.024 --> 00:07:27.777
And then she'd start talking
crap about me in Spanish.

00:07:28.528 --> 00:07:30.905
(Speaking in Spanish)

00:07:30.905 --> 00:07:32.073
(Laughs)

00:07:32.949 --> 00:07:34.701
(Speaking in Spanish)

00:07:34.742 --> 00:07:36.411
(Laughter)

00:07:36.411 --> 00:07:37.412
(Laughs)

00:07:37.412 --> 00:07:39.622
I know I’m loca. You too, huh?

00:07:39.622 --> 00:07:40.790
"No, me no."

00:07:40.832 --> 00:07:43.501
(Laughter)

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:49.215
(Speaking in Spanish)

00:07:50.091 --> 00:07:54.262
(Speaking in Spanish)

00:07:54.637 --> 00:07:56.264
What? The tone changed.

00:07:56.264 --> 00:07:57.890
What are you two saying over here?

00:07:57.932 --> 00:07:59.892
I don’t like this. Why are you sad now?

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:03.771
(Speaking in Spanish)

00:08:03.771 --> 00:08:05.023
What is that, boyfriend?

00:08:05.023 --> 00:08:07.191
I don’t want one right now, I’m free.

00:08:09.068 --> 00:08:11.696
(Speaking in Spanish)

00:08:11.738 --> 00:08:13.698
(Laughter)

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:14.991
Fair enough.

00:08:15.825 --> 00:08:18.619
See, I like imitating my family
and talking about them,

00:08:18.661 --> 00:08:21.372
because that'll never get old,
that's always a part of me.

00:08:21.372 --> 00:08:23.708
Celebrities, I don't even
know them, you know?

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:25.168
But this means so much to me.

00:08:25.168 --> 00:08:28.087
I like imitating my mom,
she's a funny character.

00:08:28.713 --> 00:08:32.050
When I'm driving my car
and she's in the passenger seat,

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:33.342
she's a backseat driver,

00:08:33.384 --> 00:08:35.136
she comments on my driving,

00:08:35.136 --> 00:08:37.221
and she knows it pisses me off.

00:08:37.263 --> 00:08:40.058
So she whispers everything
about my driving,

00:08:40.058 --> 00:08:41.476
which is like, that's worse.

00:08:41.517 --> 00:08:44.395
Everything sounds so dirty
to my innocent ears.

00:08:44.854 --> 00:08:46.022
I'm driving,

00:08:46.022 --> 00:08:49.025
she's in the passenger seat
holding on to that rail, you know.

00:08:49.067 --> 00:08:50.234
She's pressing --

00:08:50.234 --> 00:08:52.570
I didn't know there was
a brake pedal on that side

00:08:52.612 --> 00:08:54.655
because she is pressing it, she's just --

00:08:54.697 --> 00:08:56.324
(Breathes sharply through teeth)

00:08:56.824 --> 00:08:58.159
(Whispering) "Slow down."

00:08:58.201 --> 00:08:59.243
(Laughter)

00:08:59.243 --> 00:09:01.454
(Whispering) "Oh, you're going too fast."

00:09:01.496 --> 00:09:03.247
(Laughter)

00:09:03.289 --> 00:09:05.333
(Whispering) "Oh, we're not in a rush."

00:09:05.374 --> 00:09:06.667
(Laughter)

00:09:06.709 --> 00:09:08.044
(Whispering) "Oh, my back."

00:09:08.086 --> 00:09:09.253
(Laughter)

00:09:09.253 --> 00:09:11.005
"Oh, there's a spot right there,

00:09:11.047 --> 00:09:13.049
right there, right there,
right there, oh."

00:09:13.091 --> 00:09:14.258
(Laughter)

00:09:14.258 --> 00:09:15.551
"You missed it."

00:09:16.385 --> 00:09:17.970
Ew, nasty.

00:09:18.012 --> 00:09:19.847
(Laughter)

00:09:19.847 --> 00:09:22.141
Now, after nine years in my journey,

00:09:22.183 --> 00:09:26.354
I did get the chance to audition
for Saturday Night Live in 2016,

00:09:26.354 --> 00:09:28.940
and I get cast on the show.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:33.152
(Cheers and applause)

00:09:33.194 --> 00:09:36.864
It was so beautiful
to be on the show and magical,

00:09:36.906 --> 00:09:38.533
I felt like I entered ...

00:09:38.574 --> 00:09:40.409
I mean, my dream, it was real.

00:09:40.451 --> 00:09:41.577
It was ...

00:09:42.411 --> 00:09:43.746
It was beautiful.

00:09:44.413 --> 00:09:47.959
And being on SNL amplified
everything I ever wanted,

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.086
especially for doing voices.

00:09:50.128 --> 00:09:53.965
Now, I left SNL after six seasons
on the show, just recently,

00:09:54.006 --> 00:09:55.383
because, one,

00:09:55.424 --> 00:09:58.553
I wasn't strong enough anymore
to handle the pressure of the show.

00:09:59.011 --> 00:10:00.221
Two,

00:10:00.221 --> 00:10:02.849
I wasn't having fun anymore
looking up celebrities.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:07.979
And three, there was something inside me,
inside Meliss, that was saying,

00:10:07.979 --> 00:10:12.400
there's more to discover about myself,
there's more talents,

00:10:12.441 --> 00:10:15.778
there's more things
to learn, to expand on.

00:10:15.778 --> 00:10:19.699
So now I'm in a funny position
because I did the --

00:10:20.283 --> 00:10:21.450
Evil laugh.

00:10:21.450 --> 00:10:22.910
(Imitates evil laugh)

00:10:22.952 --> 00:10:24.871
(Laughter)

00:10:25.621 --> 00:10:27.415
No, but it is a funny position I'm in

00:10:27.456 --> 00:10:30.501
because that was the goal
I worked for since 15

00:10:30.543 --> 00:10:32.920
and it's so like, now, like, what do I do?

00:10:32.962 --> 00:10:36.591
Has anyone here reached a life goal
and still have years left?

00:10:36.632 --> 00:10:39.427
(Laughter and applause)

00:10:40.178 --> 00:10:43.055
There was one day recently, I Googled

00:10:43.097 --> 00:10:46.350
"What the hell do Olympians do
after they go to the Olympics?"

00:10:46.392 --> 00:10:49.312
Just because I want to know
other people that feel this way.

00:10:49.812 --> 00:10:54.942
I did find out on Google,
Olympians become teachers and mentors.

00:10:54.984 --> 00:10:56.152
And I thought,

00:10:56.194 --> 00:10:58.196
"Well, eff that. I don't want to do that."

00:10:58.196 --> 00:10:59.864
(Laughter)

00:10:59.906 --> 00:11:04.368
The thing I noticed
within the six years of being on SNL,

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:06.996
there was something -- 
the best stuff that I did

00:11:06.996 --> 00:11:10.124
were pieces where I was doing
my impressions,

00:11:10.166 --> 00:11:12.376
but I was also very much being Melissa.

00:11:12.877 --> 00:11:15.421
So as I go forth in my journey,

00:11:15.463 --> 00:11:19.300
I've got to remember to always share
the gifts that I have of doing voices

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:22.470
and also make sure I could be
vulnerable and be myself.

00:11:22.887 --> 00:11:26.265
So something I love to share
at my standup shows is

00:11:26.265 --> 00:11:28.059
how I struggle with low self-esteem,

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:32.188
and I constantly have to tell myself
positive talk and affirmations.

00:11:32.188 --> 00:11:33.981
Now I don't use my voice.

00:11:34.023 --> 00:11:36.901
No, I sound too sarcastic,
I don't believe me.

00:11:36.943 --> 00:11:38.402
(Laughter)

00:11:38.444 --> 00:11:40.613
If I say, "I'm good
at what I do, I'm funny."

00:11:40.655 --> 00:11:41.989
I don't ... no.

00:11:42.031 --> 00:11:45.326
Thankfully, I have
a Dolly Parton impression,

00:11:45.368 --> 00:11:48.162
so I say my affirmations as Dolly.

00:11:48.204 --> 00:11:49.372
Works way better.

00:11:49.413 --> 00:11:51.499
“I’m good at what I do.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:52.833
I work hard.”

00:11:52.875 --> 00:11:53.960
(Laughter)

00:11:54.001 --> 00:11:57.296
(Singing) I work nine to five.

00:11:57.296 --> 00:11:59.507
What a way to make a living.

00:11:59.507 --> 00:12:03.844
More like 10 minutes
because I’m doing a TED Talk.

00:12:03.886 --> 00:12:08.975
(Cheers and applause)

00:12:09.433 --> 00:12:13.145
So I hope the lesson
or thing you leave with

00:12:13.187 --> 00:12:16.857
is that I hope you could put
your masks down, your personas,

00:12:16.899 --> 00:12:20.569
and be your true, true self
because man, it rocks.

00:12:21.821 --> 00:12:25.616
Maybe learn a Dolly impression
so you could look in the mirrorm

00:12:25.616 --> 00:12:28.327
and say, "I am brave, I am beautiful."

00:12:28.911 --> 00:12:31.289
Or better yet, learn
your Melissa impression

00:12:31.289 --> 00:12:33.124
so you can look in the mirror and say,

00:12:33.165 --> 00:12:35.126
"Man, look at you.

00:12:35.126 --> 00:12:37.044
Yeah, you're cool."

00:12:37.503 --> 00:12:39.380
Muchas gracias, thank you.

00:12:39.422 --> 00:12:46.304
(Cheers and applause)

